<section class="cadillac-stop-system article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="cadillac-stop-system-title">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">The moving support system</p>
    <h2 id="cadillac-stop-system-title">What normally makes a car stop?</h2>
    <p>Mattar kept the Cadillac moving by assigning each ordinary stopping problem to equipment, a crew member, or a coordinated piece of the road around it.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="system-grid">
    <article>
      <h3>Human needs</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Sleep</dt><dd>Three drivers working in shifts</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Food and water</dt><dd>Stove, refrigerator, sink, drinking fountain</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Bathroom and washing</dt><dd>Toilet, shower, washing machine</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Machine needs</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Fuel, oil, coolant</dt><dd>Trailer reserves and transfer plumbing</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tire pressure</dt><dd>Air fed through drilled axles</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Flat tire or repair</dt><dd>Hydraulic lift, platform, transparent hood panels</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Road needs</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Traffic and signals</dt><dd>Police coordination and mandatory stops</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Resupply</dt><dd>Moving trucks and airfield rendezvous</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Mud and construction</dt><dd>Tractor, bulldozer, service-station loops</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="conclusion">The car did not eliminate stopping. It distributed the stop across a larger system.</p>
</section>

